WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:11.508
SafeSite Compliance Cycle. A quarterly safety-return cycle - reminders, checks, escalations and two Word reports - with nothing sent and no final overwritten.

00:00:12.517 --> 00:00:24.072
Scene 1. Twelve facilities, four coordinators, a due date and a reminder calendar. On 1 December, fourteen days before the 15 December deadline.

00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:33.592
Scene 2. Six returns arrive two weeks out. Three break a rule; each gets a correction draft. The rest get a T-14 reminder. A serious finding with no evidence,

00:00:33.592 --> 00:00:41.800
totals that do not match, and a severity that does not exist.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:50.452
Scene 3. Three days out: the corrections come back and pass. Running the same day again drafts nothing new. Each reminder is recorded once per facility and

00:00:50.452 --> 00:00:57.654
kind, so the same reminder is never drafted twice.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:06.576
Scene 4. Past the deadline, two facilities are missing. Escalations go to the coordinator with the safety lead copied, and finals are refused. Yes - drafts,

00:01:06.576 --> 00:01:14.102
marked incomplete. Finals wait.

00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:22.265
Scene 5. The late returns arrive and are accepted as late. The safety lead approves; a second approval overwrites nothing. No. They are read-only and a second

00:01:22.265 --> 00:01:29.014
approval reports ALREADY FINAL.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:40.791
Scene 6. The four folders kept apart: working, QA, final and outbox. No. Fourteen drafts wait in the outbox.

00:01:42.183 --> 00:01:45.748
The Workshop and Studio report, approved.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:52.509
The Warehouse and Depot variant is organised around open actions.

00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:59.640
A correction request: the exact problem, drafted, never sent.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:07.737
What this run showed: Each bad return refused with its reason. Reminders never duplicated, never sent. No final until every return was in. An approved final is

00:02:07.737 --> 00:02:14.023
never overwritten.
